% Origin: Kowalski, *Computational Logic and Human Thinking*,
%         Chapter 6 "The Meaning of Life", section 6.7, Examples 20-21
%         (University of Michigan lease termination clause, disambiguated).
% Last verification: no open issues (no errors/warnings; all tests pass).
%
% Two head predicates over a lessee:
%   (A) terminate with 24 hours notice -- one of five serious grounds.
%   (B) terminate with 30 days notice  -- one of five lesser grounds, BUT ONLY
%       when the 24-hours route does NOT apply to the lessee.
% This is the faithful disambiguated reading: the 30-days route is unavailable
% whenever the 24-hours route applies. Each "one of" is split into separate
% single-disjunct clauses (gotcha #6); each 30-days clause carries the guard
% "it is not the case that ... 24 hours ...".

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for *a lessee*.
the university may terminate the lease with 30 days notice for *a lessee*.
life limb or property would be jeopardized by *a lessee*.
*a lessee* deals in controlled substances.
*a lessee* is no longer enrolled.
*a lessee* possesses firearms.
*a lessee* turns in a false alarm.
*a lessee* is not eligible to enroll or fails to enroll.
*a lessee* leaves the university.
*a lessee* violates a provision of the lease.
*a lessee* violates a university regulation.
there are health reasons for terminating *a lessee*.

the knowledge base lease termination includes:

% (A) 24 hours notice -- five independent grounds.
the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for a lessee
    if life limb or property would be jeopardized by the lessee.

the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for a lessee
    if the lessee deals in controlled substances.

the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for a lessee
    if the lessee is no longer enrolled.

the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for a lessee
    if the lessee possesses firearms.

the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for a lessee
    if the lessee turns in a false alarm.

% (B) 30 days notice -- five independent grounds, each guarded by the absence
% of any 24-hours ground for the same lessee.
the university may terminate the lease with 30 days notice for a lessee
    if it is not the case that
        the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for the lessee
    and the lessee is not eligible to enroll or fails to enroll.

the university may terminate the lease with 30 days notice for a lessee
    if it is not the case that
        the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for the lessee
    and the lessee leaves the university.

the university may terminate the lease with 30 days notice for a lessee
    if it is not the case that
        the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for the lessee
    and the lessee violates a provision of the lease.

the university may terminate the lease with 30 days notice for a lessee
    if it is not the case that
        the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for the lessee
    and the lessee violates a university regulation.

the university may terminate the lease with 30 days notice for a lessee
    if it is not the case that
        the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for the lessee
    and there are health reasons for terminating the lessee.

% dan fails to enroll, with no 24-hours ground -> 30 days notice applies.
scenario dan is:
    dan is not eligible to enroll or fails to enroll.
    notice24 expects answers [].
    notice30 expects answers ["the university may terminate the lease with 30 days notice for dan"].

% eve possesses firearms (a 24h ground) AND violates a regulation (a 30-day
% ground) -> 24 hours notice; the 30-days route is blocked by the guard.
scenario eve is:
    eve possesses firearms.
    eve violates a university regulation.
    notice24 expects answers ["the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for eve"].
    notice30 expects answers [].

% Coverage scenarios exercising every remaining body predicate so that no
% template is left undefined. Each confirms the expected routing.

% frank: jeopardy + deals in substances + no longer enrolled + false alarm
% (all 24h grounds) plus leaves university + provision violation + health
% reasons (all 30-day grounds). 24h applies, so 30-day is blocked.
scenario frank is:
    life limb or property would be jeopardized by frank.
    frank deals in controlled substances.
    frank is no longer enrolled.
    frank turns in a false alarm.
    frank leaves the university.
    frank violates a provision of the lease.
    there are health reasons for terminating frank.
    notice24 expects answers ["the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for frank"].
    notice30 expects answers [].

% grace: only 30-day grounds, no 24h ground -> 30 days notice applies.
scenario grace is:
    grace leaves the university.
    grace violates a provision of the lease.
    there are health reasons for terminating grace.
    notice24 expects answers [].
    notice30 expects answers ["the university may terminate the lease with 30 days notice for grace"].

query notice24 is:
    the university may terminate the lease with 24 hours notice for which lessee.

query notice30 is:
    the university may terminate the lease with 30 days notice for which lessee.
